to each other at the time of their second marriages to other individuals. Therefore, option D is the correct answer that best fits the definition of bigamy provided in the context.\n</think>.\n<answer>Therefore, my final reasoning is that option D fits the definition of bigamy more clearly because it explicitly shows that Sun was married to Zhou and then married another woman, and Zhou was married to Sun and then married another man. Both Sun and Zhou were married to each other at the time of their second marriages to other individuals, which aligns with the definition of bigamy.</answer>",
