      "text": " C) **Environmental factors will affect the decay rate of genetic materials such as dna**.\n   - This option directly addresses the half-life of DNA sequences mentioned in the context. If environmental factors can affect the decay rate, it suggests that the half-life of DNA sequences might be more variable and less predictable than the fixed 158,000 years mentioned. This variability could potentially make it more feasible to reconstruct dinosaurs using ancient DNA, as the decay rate might not be as consistent as assumed.\n\nD) **The sequence of base pairs of dinornis and dinosaur is different**.\n   - This option is irrelevant to the half-life of DNA sequences and does not provide any information about the feasibility of reconstructing dinosaurs using ancient DNA.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the one that most directly refutes the scientist's point of view is option C, as it introduces variability in the decay rate of DNA sequences, which could make the process more feasible.\n</think>\n<answer>C</answer>",
