messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n3D stereoscopic technology represents the cutting-edge level of the current film technology, because the film to achieve a highly credible sense of space, it may become the mainstream of future films. Although the screen characters in 3D movies are computer-generated, the performances of computer characters that include actions and expressions are based on the performances of real actors, just like makeup technology in the digital age. This has also aroused the concern of some actors: with the development of computer technology, computer-generated images and animations will replace live-action performances in the future.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, can most reduce the actor's worries?\n# Options:\nA) All film directors can only communicate with real people, not with computers\nB) The shooting of any film depends on the choice of the producer, and the actors can keep up with the development of the times\nC) The current high box office of 3d movies is only the result of people's temporary novelty, and the future is still unknown\nD) The film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, and its form of expression has nothing to do with the preferences of the director", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option most effectively reduces the actor's concerns about the future of live-action performances in 3D movies. Let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) All film directors can only communicate with real people, not with computers.\n- This option suggests that directors will continue to work with real actors, which might alleviate the actor's worries. However, it doesn't directly address the concern about the future of live-action performances being replaced by computer-generated images and animations.\n\nB) The shooting of any film depends on the choice of the producer, and the actors can keep up with the development of the times.\n- This option implies that producers will continue to choose actors for live-action roles, and actors can adapt to new technologies. This directly addresses the actor's concern by suggesting that live-action performances will remain a viable option.\n\nC) The current high box office of 3d movies is only the result of people's temporary novelty, and the future is still unknown. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
