perty values**\n     - This option suggests that the park will negatively impact property values. However, the context does not provide any information that indicates the park will decrease property values. In fact, parks can increase property values by providing better amenities and a more attractive environment.\n   - **Option D: Reduced noise pollution**\n     - This option suggests that the park will reduce noise pollution. While parks can help reduce noise pollution by providing green spaces and natural barriers, the context does not specifically mention noise pollution as a benefit.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Among the given options, the one that best fits the potential benefits of the new park as mentioned in the context is Option B: Improved air quality.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.\n</think>.\n<answer>B</answer>",
