messages:   62%|######1   | 370/600 [56:16<10:33,  2.76s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, as tourism exploration has become more and more popular by some people, there are more and more rescue operations. Should we charge for the deployment of public resources to rescue tourism explorers who commit intentional adventures? These issues have also become the topic that everyone is most concerned about. The positive side thinks that it should be charged; the opposite side thinks that it should not be charged.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, cannot support the positive side's point of view?\n# Options:\nA) A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers\nB) The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support\nC) It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility\nD) Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers' money should bear the corresponding expenses", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the options provided. The context discusses whether there should be charges for deploying public resources to rescue tourists who engage in intentional adventures. The positive side believes that charges should be implemented, while the opposite side opposes this idea. We need to identify which option does not support the positive side\'s point of view.\n\nLet\'s examine each option:.\n\nA) "A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers.".\n- This statement aligns with the positive side\'s argument. It suggests that tourists should bear the cost of their actions, as they are responsible for their own decisions.\n\nB) "The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support.".\n- This statement supports the positive side\'s argument. It implies that the rescue operations require funding, and charging tourists could help cover these costs.\n\nC) "It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. Simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility.".\n- This statement opposes the positive side\'s argument. It argues that charging tourists would not encourage them to develop a sense of social responsibility, which is contrary to the positive side\'s view.\n\nD) "Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers\' money should bear the corresponding expenses.".\n- This statement supports the positive side\'s argument. It suggests that tourists who engage in risky behavior should pay for the rescue operations, as they are responsible for their actions.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, we can conclude that option C cannot support the positive side\'s point of view. It argues against the idea of charging tourists by suggesting that it would not foster a sense of social responsibility.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
