rrect.\n\n   - **Option C: Nano is a very advanced technology and has been widely used in many fields of production and life**.\n     - The context does not provide information about the widespread use of nano technology in various fields.\n     - While nano technology is indeed advanced and has applications in many fields, the given context does not support this claim.\n     - This statement is not supported by the provided information.\n\n   - **Option D: Nano usually refers to structures with very tiny dimensions**.\n     - The context defines nanostructure as "a microstructure with a size below 100 nanometers.".\n     - This statement aligns with the definition provided in the context.\n     - Therefore, this statement is correct.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Option A is correct because nano is indeed a unit of length.\n   - Option D is correct because nano usually refers to structures with very tiny dimensions. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
