s they focus on the social aspects of communication rather than the literal content.\n\nNow, let's evaluate each option based on these criteria:.\n\nA) **Have the ability to learn independently**:.\n   - This option suggests independence and self-reliance, which directly contradicts the definition of field dependence. Field dependence involves relying on external factors, not on one's own internal processing.\n\nB) **Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others**:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
