 B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal) and Qian Hong (Tsinghua) - Both correct.\n- Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking) and Sun Jie (Tsinghua) - Both correct.\n\nThe only way to satisfy the condition is if exactly one guess is correct. Let's re-evaluate the guesses:\n\n- If Zhao Ming is admitted to Tsinghua University, then Classmate A is correct, and Classmate B and Classmate C are incorrect.\n- If Zhao Ming is admitted to Beijing Normal University, then Classmate B is correct, and Classmate A and Classmate C are incorrect.\n- If Zhao Ming is admitted to Peking University, then Classmate C is correct, and Classmate A and Classmate B are incorrect.\n\nGiven that only one guess can be correct, the correct combination must be:\n- Zhao Ming to Tsinghua University.\n- Qian Hong to Beijing Normal University.\n- Sun Jie to Peking University.\n\nThus, the correct option is: D.\n</think>\n<answer>D</answer>",
