te an institutional environment for mass entrepreneurship and innovation.\n- The context mentions that China has implemented reforms to create such an environment. This is a valid point, but it seems to be a general statement rather than the main emphasis.\n\nB) The main body of entrepreneurship will move from the elite to the public.\n- The context does mention the rise of entrepreneurship from the elite to the public, but this is presented as a strong signal rather than the main emphasis.\n\nC) Mechanism and system hinder the realization of human value.\n- The context explicitly states that there are contradictions in laws, regulations, and policies, and that imperfect mechanisms and systems hinder the realization of human value. This is a significant point and aligns well with the overall message.\n\nD) Protecting people's value is the premise of mass entrepreneurship and innovation. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
